  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 760059cf5b1bb5149ae86fcc3aa6247e, type: 3}
  m_Name: NPC 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogueLines:
  - Stop right there! One more step forward and you're in danger!
  - No matter what your purpose is, don't go forward. It's dangerous.
  - The ancient tree has been going crazy for a long time...
  - Step back... Otherwise, you'll get hurt.
  - But you look like the one who came for help... That's great.
  - The forest is dangerous because of the madness of the ancient tree.
  - We tried to stop it, but all the soldiers are injured.
  - We still need timbers for the queen...
  - Now everything is messed up... What should we do?
  - Got it... I think we've made the situation worse.
  - Got it... I think we've made the situation worse.
  - To be honest, I regret being the one who cut those trees down.
  - We didn't intentionally cut them. No one wants to log in this beautiful forest.
  - These are orders from the queen. We need timbers for new walls.
  - Everyone wants to protect the kingdom... but not this way.
  - Telling the queen to stop means betraying her, doesn't it?
  - Never mind... The ancient tree went crazy because of us.
  - It's harming so many things. My fellow soldiers are injured too.
  - I was so afraid of it that I ran far away.
  - I feel so guilty toward my mates... I couldn't save them from danger.
  - Tell me... Am I a good soldier?
  - Fine... I have to stay here and take care of those who are injured.
  - The ancient tree doesn't listen to anyone now. You should be careful.
  - Go stop the ancient tree. For the kingdom and the forest.
